1
00:00:00,080 --> 00:00:02,090
The day is shrinking fast.

2
00:00:02,598 --> 00:00:05,338
Now the spin
begins to speed up.

3
00:00:05,653 --> 00:00:08,978
At 20 hours, you can see
the shadows sweep.

4
00:00:09,587 --> 00:00:14,112
At 16, the Sun climbs the
sky like a slow elevator.

5
00:00:14,820 --> 00:00:17,300
A day only ever
gets shorter,

6
00:00:17,390 --> 00:00:19,385
and you cannot
turn it back.

7
00:00:19,727 --> 00:00:24,297
At a 12 hour day, sunrise
to sunset takes 6 hours.

8
00:00:24,853 --> 00:00:28,863
At a 12 hour day the Sun
moves across the sky

9
00:00:28,863 --> 00:00:32,058
as fast as the hour
hand on a clock.

10
00:00:32,648 --> 00:00:35,418
The ground under
your feet now moves

11
00:00:35,418 --> 00:00:39,458
at about 3,300 kilometers
an hour,

12
00:00:39,458 --> 00:00:42,623
nearly three times
the speed of sound.

13
00:00:43,320 --> 00:00:47,880
You weigh 1.4 percent less
than on a still Earth,

14
00:00:47,880 --> 00:00:50,335
four times what you
feel today.

15
00:00:51,258 --> 00:00:53,023
Quick break:
like and follow.

16
00:00:53,263 --> 00:00:55,578
Then let's see
how bad this gets.

17
00:00:56,348 --> 00:01:00,348
8 hours of sleep no longer
fits inside one night.

18
00:01:00,813 --> 00:01:02,983
And then the wind
starts to blow.

19
00:01:03,485 --> 00:01:05,215
Part two of eight.
